  {
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "@gmarkall, the note on broadcasted array has to be contiguous is correct. The emitted kernel is expecting the outer-dims (looped-over axes) are flattened so it can do a 1-D kernel configuration.  I tried a hack to make sure the outer-dims are flatten in a 1-D loop and it seems to work for this case. \r\n\r\nSee patch in https://gist.github.com/sklam/57ef1bfb4a1885c4309d1a4c706dab33 which is based on https://github.com/gmarkall/numba/commit/ae96876cb29242699bfb904c2614300a3b9922f8\r\n\r\n",
